A||||3||Rare87GT||Trying to swap rims from a GTP to Fiero||||1||
Z||000000||Rare87GT||11-05-2001||06:32 PM||||Got a question for you guys.  I have an 85 Pontiac 6000 with GTP 16" rims that I am trying to swap onto my 87 Fiero but the lug nut pattern was different so I was forced to try and swap hubs with the 6000 and put them on the Fiero.  Well come to find out I guess that the suspension in the back is different.  The Fiero's is independent and the 6000 is separate.  I really want to get these rims on the Fiero but don't know how the heck to do it.  And I really don't want to get hub adapters so the lug nut pattern will fit.  Any ideas guys?  Thanks.<P>------------------<BR>1987 GT (Canadian)||||reg||1
Z||000001||TRiAD||11-05-2001||06:41 PM||||Why no adapters? If you're not going to be braking and cornering at 10/10ths at 130+MPH, there's no problem. <P>...and if you are, take vidoe and post it!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Also, there are companies that make them for racing applications. <P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0NgAlAL0S2vLvViYU9P7uloj72fLFTqfz59trng8I7AOG7hGCvfk6WP96n!gnOaEUAvooy1kUoWucv7BJ7L5EWg/temp-sig.gif">    <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||11-05-2001||07:35 PM||||You're talking big money. The 115mm bolt pattern of the bigger wheels changes lots of parts. The front's will be the challenge. On the rears, the bearing, outer CV and knuckle will need to be changed. They all go together. You might be able to put the 6000 front knuckles on. The larger CV's use the manual trans diameter axle shaft.<P>In the front, that's a problem. What RWD cars came with 115mm spacing in front......Thinking.......thinking......think......thin.......thi........th......t...............I'm tapped.....||||reg||1
Z||000003||Rare87GT||11-05-2001||07:59 PM||||The wheel adapters are like $300.  I would get them, but I just wanted to be sure there was no way to get the rims on the Fiero without having to buy the adapter to get them on.  ||||reg||1
